"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15GraphOperations12SubgraphViewV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"spanningSubgraphView(edges:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/TransposedView\/spanningSubgraphView(edges:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/transposedview\/spanningsubgraphview(edges:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The spanning subgraph with the edges at "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": every vertex, at its own index, and only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those edges, as a lazy view (igraph’s "},{"code":"subgraph_edges(delete_vertices=False)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"FilterArcs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). A position listed twice is kept once. The view has dense edge indices, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge’s rank among the kept edges in the graph’s order."}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/TransposedView/inducedSubgraphView(on:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/TransposedView\/inducedSubgraphView(on:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The subgraph induced by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":": those vertices and every edge between them, as a lazy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view (igraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"induced_subgraph"},{"type":"text","text":", NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G.subgraph(nodes)"},{"type":"text","text":"). The kept vertices are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numbered in the graph’s order, whatever the listed order; a vertex listed twice is kept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once. The vi